					<li Class="Message">
						<def>ThreatBig</def>
						<ID>57</ID>
						<text>Mechanoids have woken up.</text>
						<startingTime>50212.0508</startingTime>
						<startingFrame>2985844</startingFrame>
						<startingTick>763828</startingTick>
						<lookTargets>
							<targets>
								<li>null</li>
							</targets>
						</lookTargets>
						<quest>null</quest>
					</li>
					<li Class="StandardLetter">
						<ID>57</ID>
						<def>NeutralEvent</def>
						<label>The thrusters were on the EAST flank venting</label>
						<lookTargets>
							<targets>
								<li>(91, 0, 150), Map_0</li>
							</targets>
						</lookTargets>
						<relatedFaction>null</relatedFaction>
						<arrivalTick>764388</arrivalTick>
						<text>The thrusters were on the EAST flank venting east - she was built to fly left. They are on the west wall line now, facing east, and the wall they left is back. She flies right.</text>
						<quest>null</quest>
						<hyperlinkThingDefs IsNull="True" />
						<hyperlinkHediffDefs IsNull="True" />
					</li>
					<li Class="StandardLetter">
						<ID>59</ID>
						<def>NeutralEvent</def>
						<label>Hull colour is MATERIAL, not paint - MegaBon</label>
						<lookTargets>
							<targets>
								<li>(127, 0, 154), Map_0</li>
							</targets>
						</lookTargets>
						<relatedFaction>null</relatedFaction>
						<arrivalTick>764388</arrivalTick>
						<text>Hull colour is MATERIAL, not paint - MegaBone where the plating is sound, DinoChitin where it is corroding. The dev Set Color tool runs out after ~380 calls per session; material never does and survives a reload.</text>
						<quest>null</quest>
						<hyperlinkThingDefs IsNull="True" />
						<hyperlinkHediffDefs IsNull="True" />
					</li>
					<li Class="StandardLetter">
						<ID>56</ID>
						<def>NeutralEvent</def>
						<label>Every bay carries an Aurebesh word for what </label>
						<lookTargets>
							<targets>
								<li>(146, 0, 182), Map_0</li>
							</targets>
						</lookTargets>
						<relatedFaction>null</relatedFaction>
						<arrivalTick>764388</arrivalTick>
						<text>Every bay carries an Aurebesh word for what it USED to be. SMELTING, REFINERY, MEDICAL, KITCHEN, FARMING, ARMORY, CONTROL, REACTOR, COMMAND, CARGO, ENGINEER, STORAGE, LANDING. That is the floor telling you the ship's history.</text>
						<quest>null</quest>
						<hyperlinkThingDefs IsNull="True" />
						<hyperlinkHediffDefs IsNull="True" />
					</li>
					<li Class="StandardLetter">
						<ID>55</ID>
						<def>NeutralEvent</def>
						<label>Both feet were sealed square rooms. They are</label>
						<lookTargets>
							<targets>
								<li>(117, 0, 65), Map_0</li>
							</targets>
						</lookTargets>
						<relatedFaction>null</relatedFaction>
						<arrivalTick>764388</arrivalTick>
						<text>Both feet were sealed square rooms. They are landing pads now - side and bottom walls cut back to corner stubs, grate apron, a real shuttle pad and four beacons. The ship LANDS rather than sits.</text>
						<quest>null</quest>
						<hyperlinkThingDefs IsNull="True" />
						<hyperlinkHediffDefs IsNull="True" />
					</li>
					<li Class="StandardLetter">
						<ID>52</ID>
						<def>NeutralEvent</def>
						<label>The palette. Rusted biotech tile is the conn</label>
						<lookTargets>
							<targets>
								<li>(126, 0, 176), Map_0</li>
							</targets>
						</lookTargets>
						<relatedFaction>null</relatedFaction>
						<arrivalTick>764388</arrivalTick>
						<text>The palette. Rusted biotech tile is the connective tissue and reaches everywhere. Iron plating means heavy industry. Crossed grate iron means the deck plating is GONE - it is damage, not trim. Divoted rust is held back for the spine and used nowhere else.</text>
						<quest>null</quest>
						<hyperlinkThingDefs IsNull="True" />
						<hyperlinkHediffDefs IsNull="True" />
					</li>
					<li Class="StandardLetter">
						<ID>53</ID>
						<def>NeutralEvent</def>
						<label>37 blisters, grown from a seeded noise field</label>
						<lookTargets>
							<targets>
								<li>(104, 0, 180), Map_0</li>
							</targets>
						</lookTargets>
						<relatedFaction>null</relatedFaction>
						<arrivalTick>764388</arrivalTick>
						<text>37 blisters, grown from a seeded noise field rather than placed by hand, so they read as corrosion instead of decoration. 546 cells of missing plating.</text>
						<quest>null</quest>
						<hyperlinkThingDefs IsNull="True" />
						<hyperlinkHediffDefs IsNull="True" />
					</li>
					<li Class="StandardLetter">
						<ID>54</ID>
						<def>NeutralEvent</def>
						<label>The eight biggest blisters ate through the S</label>
						<lookTargets>
							<targets>
								<li>(157, 0, 92), Map_0</li>
							</targets>
						</lookTargets>
						<relatedFaction>null</relatedFaction>
						<arrivalTick>764388</arrivalTick>
						<text>The eight biggest blisters ate through the SUBSTRATE too - foundation stripped, 140 cells. You are looking at the ground through the ship. The pod is the worst of them and its stalk is cut.</text>
						<quest>null</quest>
						<hyperlinkThingDefs IsNull="True" />
						<hyperlinkHediffDefs IsNull="True" />
					</li>
					<li Class="StandardLetter">
						<ID>58</ID>
						<def>NeutralEvent</def>
						<label>REFINERY, KITCHEN and ARMORY have been gutte</label>
						<lookTargets>
							<targets>
								<li>(107, 0, 181), Map_0</li>
							</targets>
						</lookTargets>
						<relatedFaction>null</relatedFaction>
						<arrivalTick>764388</arrivalTick>
						<text>REFINERY, KITCHEN and ARMORY have been gutted - machines destroyed, replaced with ruins, slag and machine-bits. The Aurebesh word STAYS. A sign outliving its factory is the whole story of this ship.</text>
						<quest>null</quest>
						<hyperlinkThingDefs IsNull="True" />
						<hyperlinkHediffDefs IsNull="True" />
					</li>
