						<name>Plunderism</name>
						<adjective>plunderic</adjective>
						<memberName>Plunderer</memberName>
						<leaderTitleMale>Solemn Chief</leaderTitleMale>
						<leaderTitleFemale>Solemn Chief</leaderTitleFemale>
						<description>"Homage to thee, O thou glorious Being, thou who art provided with all things. O Tmu-Heru-khuti, when thou risest in the horizon of heaven, a cry cometh out of the mouth of all peoples: What you can't defend doesn't belong to you. If anyone disagrees, I'm always ready to defend myself. I have rested in Hemet, on the north of the field of the grasshoppers, wherein the holy mariners do purify themselves in the night season."

  - Fragment of a recovered papyrus found in the black market of Irithir</description>
						<descriptionTemplate>"Homage to thee, O thou glorious Being, thou who art provided with all things. O Tmu-Heru-khuti, when thou risest in the horizon of heaven, a cry cometh out of the mouth of all peoples: What you can't defend doesn't belong to you. If anyone disagrees, I'm always ready to defend myself. I have rested in Hemet, on the north of the field of the grasshoppers, wherein the holy mariners do purify themselves in the night season."

  - Fragment of a recovered papyrus found in the black market of Irithir</descriptionTemplate>
