						<solid>True</solid>
						<id>29</id>
						<development IsNull="True" />
					</li>
					<li>
						<foundation Class="IdeoFoundation_Deity">
							<def>Deity</def>
							<place>Yttak</place>
							<deities>
								<li>
									<name>Christ-Lord</name>
									<type>All-Powerful God</type>
									<gender>Male</gender>
									<iconPath>UI/Deities/DeityGeneric</iconPath>
									<relatedMeme>HumanPrimacy</relatedMeme>
								</li>
							</deities>
						</foundation>
						<name>Perfect Army</name>
						<adjective>Anthro-Methodist</adjective>
						<memberName>Anthro-Methodist</memberName>
						<leaderTitleMale>High Chief</leaderTitleMale>
						<leaderTitleFemale>High Chief</leaderTitleFemale>
						<description>Anthro-Methodists built a great &lt;color=#D09B61FF&gt;Perfect Logo&lt;/color&gt; on the ice-moon prison Yttak, and filled it with sugary sweets to serve to any visiting pilgrims. A prison warden passed a law forbidding Anthro-Methodists from rising to the ruling classes of Yttak. A warrior named Eyfriðr Dórisdóttir used an archotech mass-inverter to destroy a guard barracks. &lt;color=#D09B61FF&gt;Christ-Lord&lt;/color&gt; saw Eyfriðr's ruthlessness and anointed her the rightful ruler of all humanity. Because of Eyfriðr's actions, the prison warden's corrupt guards saw &lt;color=#D09B61FF&gt;Christ-Lord&lt;/color&gt;'s truth. They celebrated their shared humanity with the Anthro-Methodists and banished the prison warden to live in the wilderness like an animal.</description>
						<descriptionTemplate>%%MemberNamePlural%% built a great %%altar0_name%% on the ice-moon prison Yttak, and filled it with sugary sweets to serve to any visiting pilgrims. A prison warden passed a law forbidding %%memberNamePlural%% from rising to the ruling classes of Yttak. A warrior named Eyfriðr Dórisdóttir used an archotech mass-inverter to destroy a guard barracks. %%Deity0_name%% saw Eyfriðr's ruthlessness and anointed her the rightful ruler of all humanity. Because of Eyfriðr's actions, the prison warden's corrupt guards saw %%deity0_name%%'s truth. They celebrated their shared humanity with the %%memberNamePlural%% and banished the prison warden to live in the wilderness like an animal.</descriptionTemplate>
						<culture>BS_MedievalCulture</culture>
						<iconDef>ReligionC</iconDef>
						<colorDef>Purple</colorDef>
						<primaryFactionColor>RGBA(0.190, 0.150, 0.100, 1.000)</primaryFactionColor>
						<memes>
							<li>Structure_OriginChristian</li>
							<li>Supremacist</li>
							<li>HumanPrimacy</li>
							<li>VME_SweetTeeth</li>
						</memes>
