						<description>A contract is the only honest thing two strangers can hold between them. It names one person, one price, one ending, and everyone not written into it walks away untouched. We do not pillage — pillage is confessing you could not find the one you came for. Take the mark or refuse it in the open. Once it is taken it is finished, or you are.</description>
						<descriptionTemplate>"It is thus that we learn one single truth: "You must live being true to the single purpose of the present moment". The most important thing I've learned is that you never appreciate your anonymity until you don't have it anymore. But that was only my path - What will yours be?"

  - &lt;i&gt;Reflections by a Penitent Farm Hand&lt;/i&gt; by Norman Cordova</descriptionTemplate>
						<culture>Jawa_Culture_Blackstar</culture>
						<iconDef>AbstractsC</iconDef>
